# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Astronomy Open Night 2026 — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and pass with:
#   flutter run --dart-define-from-file=.env
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️  THE APP CURRENTLY NEEDS NONE OF THIS.
#
# `flutter run` works with no .env file at all. Every screen runs on
# data compiled into the binary, and the map uses OpenStreetMap raster
# tiles, which require no API key.
#
# This file exists to (a) document that absence deliberately, so nobody
# assumes a missing key is why something is broken, and (b) give the
# variables a home if the situations below ever arise.
#
# Do NOT copy values from the MQ Journey repository into here. That
# project's Supabase, Firebase and Transport for NSW credentials belong
# to a different product and must not be reused.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Build environment label. One of: development | staging | production
APP_ENV=development

# ── Optional: alternative map tiles ────────────────────────
# Only needed if the OSM public tile servers prove too slow or the
# Tile Usage Policy becomes a concern at event scale (see the "Known
# limitations" section of README.md). Leave blank to use OSM.
#
# MAP_TILE_URL_TEMPLATE=
# MAP_TILE_API_KEY=

# ── Deliberately absent ────────────────────────────────────
# There is no auth, no user accounts, no analytics and no backend in
# this MVP, so there are no keys for any of them. If you find yourself
# adding one, that is a scope change worth discussing first — see
# docs/project-scope.md.
